  "notation": "Env-Wq 1502.55",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1502.55 Redevelopment",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1502.55 “Redevelopment” means to undertake construction on property where development activities occurred more than 10 years prior to the proposed development activities and where the area of existing impervious cover is 60% or greater of the area of the property, including any abutting properties under the control of the property owner.\n\nSource. #13758, eff 9-28-23; ss by #14472, eff 1-19-26, EXPIRES: 1-19-36; renumbered by #14656, eff 8-6-26, EXPIRES: 8-6-36 (formerly Env-Wq 1502.53)",
